to-be-incorporated-into-paper-124 = unlines (cons "In hyperactivity's language as the repository implements it: **Recursion.** A call on a field of the matched argument is structural, applied to all its later" (cons "arguments or to fewer (a partial call is the function of the rest: `lapp (f k)` passes it); a definition at a type with" (cons "a clock recurses through any functions where a later value is expected (“Guarded recursion” in “The language as implemented” (docs/to-be-incorporated-into-paper.cub)). A call on a field's field," (cons "at any depth (`fib (suc (suc n)) = plus (fib n) (fib (suc n))`), is course-of-values: the split" (cons "computes each value together with the values below it (a Σ of the value and `Below v`, `Below`" (cons "itself an elimination into types), and a split of a variable below reverts that pair, so that in" (cons "its branches `Below` unfolds to the pairs of its own recursive fields. Any other terminating" (cons "recursion is written with a measure into `Nat` and, where the obligation does not compute to" (cons "`Unit`, a proof of it:" (cons "" (cons "```" (cons "zig : (a b : Nat) → Nat" (cons "zig zero b = b" (cons "zig (suc a) b = suc (zig b a)" (cons "decreasing by plus a b using <-suc-eq (plus b a) (plus a b) (plus-comm b a)" (cons "```" nil))))))))))))))))
